# Product First — Development Gate

Infrastructure is complete. **No new systems** unless they directly improve the customer experience.

**Business model:** `docs/BUSINESS_MODEL.md` (LOCKED — two products only)

**Builder Pass UX:** `docs/BUILDER_JOURNEY.md` — guided journey, not course/docs. See `.cursor/rules/builder-pass-product-rule.mdc`

## Every task must improve at least one of:

1. **Learning** — short checkpoints that enable building (not reading)
2. **Building** — missions, guided workflows, real output
3. **Customer transformation** — Learn → Build → Complete → Continue loop; upgrade readiness

If a task does not clearly map to one of the above → **backlog**. Do not implement.

## Builder Pass page gate

Before shipping any Builder Pass screen:

- Creates **momentum**, not documentation
- Has one clear **primary action**
- Matches **onboarding UX** (`/start-here` + `vault-ui.tsx`)
- Feels like **completing a mission**, not consuming content

If it fails → redesign, do not ship as-is.

## Backlog (do not build without explicit request)

- New pricing tiers (Lite, Enterprise, Teams)
- Stripe / webhooks (unless blocking real sales)
- Affiliate attribution, fraud, payout APIs, queues, Redis
- Analytics platforms, heatmaps, event sourcing
- Supabase migration (unless blocking content delivery)
- Landing page CRO / marketing polish
- New admin infrastructure unrelated to journey content
- Email automations, community platforms
- LMS-style course infrastructure (modules, video players, quizzes)

## Allowed without asking

- Mission-driven Builder Journey pages
- First Build Mission walkthrough
- Setup wizard → Mission 1 path
- Transform `/vault/start` into journey entry (mission framing)
- Bug fixes that block learning or building

## Frozen systems (bug fixes only)

- Business Model V1 — `business-model-locked.mdc`
- Landing page V1 — `landing-frozen.mdc`
- Onboarding wizard — `onboarding-frozen.mdc` (feeling is benchmark; copy frozen)
- Affiliate Center V1 — `affiliate-center-frozen.mdc`

## North star

**Builder Pass qualifies buyers through missions. Monthly Build Pro ($29/mo) is the primary business.**

See `docs/BUILDER_JOURNEY.md` for UX standard and `docs/AI_INCOME_BUILDER_COURSE.md` for Mission 1 content outline.
